# llama.cpp Service Configuration

The OJU Video Forge inference layer supports both Ollama and llama.cpp as inference providers. This compose overlay enables optional llama.cpp service deployment.

## Usage

Add to your compose stack:

```yaml
include:
  - compose.llamacpp.yaml
```

Environment variables required:

```
LLAMA_CPP_ENABLED=true
LLAMA_CPP_URL=http://llama-cpp:8080
LLAMA_CPP_MODEL=mistral-latest  # or qwen2.5:7b-instruct GGUF
```

## Image Selection

Use official llama.cpp CUDA server image:

```yaml
image: ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:server-cuda@sha256:<DIGEST>
```

Select a pinned digest from https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases or similar.

## Configuration Notes

- No published host ports - service runs on internal `agent-inference` network only
- Uses separate GGUF model storage directory (`/models`)
- GPU allocation via Docker gpus: all directive
- Context size configurable via environment variables
- Health check based on `/v1/models` endpoint availability